  "configuration_id": "config_038",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best configuration so far is config_032 (scvi_n200 + resnet50, multiprofile, transformer, concat) at 0.688 acc, but image-only resnet50 performs very poorly (0.208 acc), raising uncertainty about whether the image modality is contributing meaningful signal or just noise that happens to complement RNA. Question: config_038 isolates the image encoder choice by swapping resnet50 for imagenet_vit_l while holding all other settings identical to config_032 (scvi_n200, multiprofile, transformer, concat). This directly tests whether a stronger, pretrained vision transformer yields a meaningfully better image representation that improves multimodal fusion. Why this is the best next experiment: The image encoder is a fundamental design axis with high uncertainty—resnet50's poor standalone performance suggests it may be capping the multimodal ceiling. If ViT-L substantially improves over resnet50, it reshapes the entire multimodal design space and justifies further investment in the image modality; if it does not, we can conclude the image contribution is limited and focus budget on RNA-side refinements or fusion strategy. This single-variable comparison is maximally informative per experiment under the limited budget."
}

